From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:50:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: matisse3g: reserve persistent crash logging

The appended second-stage DT replaces the bootstrap's live DT. Describe
the verified lk2nd ramoops address explicitly in that DT so the page
allocator cannot reuse the region and the second-stage kernel registers
a persistent-log backend. Previous raw readback contained no valid
pstore signature or kernel console records.

Reserve 512 KiB at 0x2ff80000, keep the 256 KiB console at lk2nd's existing
0x2ffc0000 address, and allocate two 128 KiB panic records below it. The
bootstrap recovery DT must use the same layout. RAM retention still needs
a real panic/warm-restart acceptance test; this description alone does
not establish that test result.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
index dee4e58a7..9b0cd5c26 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
@@ -419,3 +419,15 @@ &cpu2 {
 &cpu3 {
 	cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_spc>;
 };
+
+/ {
+	reserved-memory {
+		ramoops@2ff80000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x2ff80000 0x80000>;
+			record-size = <0x20000>;
+			console-size = <0x40000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+	};
+};
